.TH HEARTBEAT_SENDER 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
heartbeat_sender \- send UDP heartbeats (C++ implementation)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B heartbeat_sender
.RB [ \-f | \-\-file
.IR json_file ]
.RB [ \-n | \-\-name
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-s | \-\-status
.IR status ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-p | \-\-port
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-i | \-\-interval
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-\-count
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-I | \-\-interface
.IR iface ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B heartbeat_sender
is the C++17 equivalent of
.BR heartbeat_sender.py (1),
built from
.I cpp_sender/
with CMake on top of
.BR libheartbeat_sender_lib (3).
It accepts the same options and produces heartbeats that decode to the same
JSON object, with compact separators, raw UTF\-8, and a millisecond UTC
timestamp
.RI ( YYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM:SS.mmm+00:00 ).
.PP
Unlike the Python sender, options given explicitly on the command line always
override the
.B \-\-file
values, even when they equal the defaults.
.PP
POSIX only; the program does not build on Windows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIjson_file\fR
Read
.BR name ,
.BR status ,
.BR host ,
.BR port ,
.BR interval ,
.B count
and
.B interface
from a JSON object.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fIname\fR
Sender name.
Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status " " \fIstatus\fR
Status string.
Default
.BR OK .
.TP
.BI \-\-host " host"
Destination address or host name.
Default
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIport\fR
Destination UDP port.
Default 9999.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fIseconds\fR
Send every
.I seconds
(floating point); 0 sends once.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " n"
Stop after
.I n
heartbeats in interval mode; 0 means unlimited.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-interface " " \fIiface\fR
Outgoing interface for IPv6 link\-local or multicast destinations.
An unknown interface name is an error.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print each heartbeat as it is sent.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Sent, or interval mode stopped with SIGINT.
In interval mode individual send failures are printed as warnings and do not
change the exit status.
.TP
.B 1
Missing name, unreadable or invalid JSON file, unknown option, or a one\-shot
send failure.
.TP
.B 134
A non\-numeric
.BR \-\-port ,
.B \-\-interval
or
.B \-\-count
value: the parse exception is not caught and the process aborts.
.PP
A send to a host name ignores the
.BR sendto (2)
result, so a failure there is not reported.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build and run:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
cmake \-S cpp_sender \-B cpp_sender/build
cmake \-\-build cpp_sender/build \-j
cpp_sender/build/heartbeat_sender \-\-name daq\-node\-01 \-\-host monitor\-host
cpp_sender/build/heartbeat_sender \-\-name runcontrol \-\-interval 10 \-v
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR heartbeat_sender.py (1),
.BR libheartbeat_sender_lib (3),
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor\-api (7)
